   "epithet": "The old Phrygian capital",
   "text": "The city of the Phrygian kings, under Persia since about 540, on its walled mound by the Sangarios. North of it lie the royal burial mounds; the greatest, about 53 metres high, has no art of its own here: the cemetery is shown with common mounds, the town with common pieces."
